 Summary of  QuantumSavory  tools employed in the simulation We used the  Register  and  RegisterNet  data structures to hold the switch and client qubits on a star graph, and the classical  channel  of the network to carry requests. The simulation is assembled almost entirely from high-level  QuantumSavory.ProtocolZoo  protocols: SimpleSwitchDiscreteProt  for the switch's entangling/swapping/scheduling logic; EntanglementTracker  for keeping each client's classical metadata consistent across swaps; EntanglementConsumer  for detecting and consuming finished end-to-end pairs; the  SwitchRequest / Tag  classical-messaging layer for the client requests. The only hand-written process is the small  make_request  helper. Everything else — the entanglement bookkeeping that the  low-level examples  implement by hand — is reused from the zoo. Visualization is handled by  Makie.jl  via  registernetplot_axis  and standard Makie plots, and the discrete-event scheduling by  ConcurrentSim.jl . import mermaid from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.esm.min.mjs';
